{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Re-adding a model with incompatible settings can persist a catalog that prevents the daemon from starting on restart."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A bare IPv6 SSH destination causes local management commands to fail before reaching SSH."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Resuming an interrupted mixed-target evaluation rejects the entire request when one target has been retired."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Retrying a historical run fails on a retired model reference even when its saved chain has an available fallback."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The current configuration wiring works, but the requested end-to-end status coverage is missing."},{"id":"C10","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An SSH alias or different provider port prevents automatic provider updates and can make status probe an unrelated guessed endpoint."},{"id":"C2b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Supplying an SSH option as the host can make status report an active service without contacting a server."},{"id":"C3b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Retrying a historical run rejects a retired model before its working fallback can be selected."}]}